title: Route1Start
tags: cutscene
---
// The game starts here (chart.rs FIRST_NODE): the start node of chapter R1Viewing.
// He is on the landing, at ten, for the viewing of 3B.
<<set $chapter to "R1Viewing">>
<<fade_out>>
<<card "Saturday. The viewing.">>
<<fade_in>>
<<note r1_view "Viewing: flat 3B, top floor. Saturday, ten. Knock.">>
You: 3B. Top floor. Ten o'clock.
===
title: Route1Viewing
tags: cutscene
---
<<declare $samantha_name = "_Samantha">>
<<declare $r1_viewing_why = "">>
// Started by knocking on 3B (door_3b.yarn). The door across the hall opens instead.
<<walk Player PlayerKnock>>
<<face Player up>>
<<open_door Door3A>>
<<show Samantha>>
<<walk Samantha SamanthaOut>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Nobody's in there. That's sort of the point.
You: Oh. Sorry. I'm here for the viewing.
{$samantha_name}: I know. You're six minutes early.
{$samantha_name}: Keen or nervous?
// PLACEHOLDER: replaces the opening menu.
You: ...Both?
{$samantha_name}: Honest. That's a terrible way to start a negotiation.
// She turns back to her open door for the keys (assumes 3A is south of her).
<<face Samantha down>>
{$samantha_name}: My father owns the building. He's away this week, so you get me instead.
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<set $samantha_name to "Samantha">>
{$samantha_name}: Samantha. That's my door. Whoever takes this flat gets me as a neighbour, too.
You: Nice to meet you, I'm-
{$samantha_name}: I know who you are. You sent an application. With a photo.
{$samantha_name}: Brave choice, the photo.
// She unlocks 3B and stays in the doorway.
<<walk Samantha SamanthaTo3B>>
<<face Samantha up>>
<<open_door Door3B>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Shoes off, please.
You: House rule?
{$samantha_name}: My rule. My father doesn't care.
{$samantha_name}: Interesting socks.
// The main room. She stays in the middle of it while he looks around.
<<walk Samantha SamanthaToKitchen no_wait>>
<<walk Player PlayerToKitchen>>
<<await_walks>>
<<close_door Door3B>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: This is it. Bare walls, good floor.
// PLACEHOLDER: the tour is his now.
{$samantha_name}: Window, kitchenette, bathroom. Look at whatever you like.
{$samantha_name}: Tell me when you've seen enough.
<<set $gate_r1_view_knock to true>>
<<note r1_view "Look around 3B: the window, the kitchenette, the bathroom. Then tell her.">>
===
title: Route1ViewingEnd
tags: cutscene
---
// Started by telling her he's seen enough (samantha_3a.yarn): the bottleneck of
// R1Viewing. Back on the landing, she locks up.
<<set $gate_r1_view_end to true>>
<<note_done r1_view>>
<<walk Samantha SamanthaToLanding no_wait>>
<<walk Player PlayerToLanding>>
<<await_walks>>
<<face Samantha up>>
<<close_door Door3B>>
<<face Samantha Player>>
<<face Player Samantha>>
{$samantha_name}: Anything you want to ask me?
// PLACEHOLDER: replaces the question menu.
You: When will I hear back?
{$samantha_name}: When I've decided.
You: Not your father?
{$samantha_name}: He signs whatever I hand him.
{$samantha_name}: There are two more viewings this week.
{$samantha_name}: Both of them wore matching socks.
{$samantha_name}: I'll let you know.
// She goes back through her own door.
<<walk Samantha SamanthaHome>>
<<hide Samantha>>
<<close_door Door3A>>
// Time skip to moving day (route1_movein.yarn).
<<fade_out>>
<<next_scene Route1MoveInStart>>
===
